# The zero tokens of a run `take` hands out (zero_run, their caller in
# huge; SlabTable::new is axiom_fresh_anon_zero's other; both pinned by
# huge::tests::zero_axioms_called_from_listed_sites): kernel zero-fill
# facts under the allocator's rules.
# The fresh pages: zero_run's requires tie the premise to the mark, which
# only `take` raises, and SlabTable::new mints the class region's token
# once per class, which then goes only with the slabs handed out, so what
# is left is mmap(2)'s zero fill of a private anonymous mapping that
# nothing has written since.
axiom_fresh_anon_zero	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# The Purged pages: zero_run's requires tie the premise to
# Huge::rediscard's success for the run's pages, so what is left is
# madvise(2)'s MADV_DONTNEED zero fill of a private anonymous mapping
# that nothing has written since take's rediscard call.
axiom_discarded_zero	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)	trusted (requires, checked at its one caller, zero_run, from Huge::take: some MADV_DONTNEED of exactly these bytes succeeded, `sys::madvise_ok`, at that call site Huge::rediscard's; not checked: that nothing has written them since take's rediscard call)
